{"uid":"f5c65106a97c4cb1","name":"test_worker_reentry_after_an_operator_steer_stays_on_approach_one_and_pauses_again","fullName":"tests.test_approach_start_head_persistence#test_worker_reentry_after_an_operator_steer_stays_on_approach_one_and_pauses_again","historyId":"24c57d7c5c1a277c0c350348560b8491","time":{"start":1791867496987,"stop":1791867497425,"duration":438},"description":"Requirement A.3, the literal PRD `Cured when:` sequence: commit ->\n    stagnation pause -> operator steer -> worker re-entry -> renewed\n    stagnation, still on approach 1, pause/escalation emitted both times,\n    no `approaches/NN` archive ever created.\n\n    Pre-task-001 (`_step_worker` re-deriving `approach_start_head` fresh\n    from `self._workspace_head_sha()` at its own method entry instead of\n    reading `self._approach_start_head(approach)` back) this fails at the\n    THIRD `_step_worker()` call below -- the worker RE-ENTRY that follows\n    the steer round trip: that call's own fresh local re-derives the\n    baseline from the CURRENT head, which already carries the earlier\n    commit -- so the renewed, genuinely quiet stagnation round's commit\n    witness reads as 'unchanged', a progressing-but-not-last approach is\n    wrongly treated as fully silent:\n    `('advance', 'replan', 'stagnation_exhausted')`, `approaches/01`\n    archived, `sup._approach` advanced past 1.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Requirement A.3, the literal PRD <code>Cured when:</code> sequence: commit -&gt;<br />\nstagnation pause -&gt; operator steer -&gt; worker re-entry -&gt; renewed<br />\nstagnation, still on approach 1, pause/escalation emitted both times,<br />\nno <code>approaches/NN</code> archive ever created.</p>\n<pre><code>Pre-task-001 (`_step_worker` re-deriving `approach_start_head` fresh\nfrom `self._workspace_head_sha()` at its own method entry instead of\nreading `self._approach_start_head(approach)` back) this fails at the\nTHIRD `_step_worker()` call below -- the worker RE-ENTRY t